{title: The Donkeys And The Bread}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 9:2–4; 9:9–12; 16:1–4; 16:4; 19:24–30}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bbmaj7] | [Bbmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]A servant came from Saul's old house
[Bb]Named Ziba standing in the [F]dust
[Gm]The king asked [C]if any kin re[Dm]mained
Of Jonathan's line in this [Bb]land
A [Gm]son with [C]feet that could not [Bb]walk
[Gm]Living far away [C]from the [Dm]ark
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [Bb]donkeys loaded [C]with the bread
[Dm]Two hundred loaves are spread
[Bb]Raisins and fruit [C]for the men
[Dm]Wine for the faint in the wilderness then
[Bb]Everything [C]that belongs to [Dm]Mep[C6]hi[Bb]bosheth
Is now [Gm]yours to [Am7]claim and to pos[Dm]sess
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Gm] [Am7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]David fled when Absalom rose
[Bb]Ziba met him with a [F]show
[Gm]He said the mas[Am]ter stayed be[Dm]hind
To take the kin[C]gdom from the [Bb]mind
So [Gm]the king gave [C]all the es[Bb]tate
To [Gm]Ziba who [C]bowed before the [Dm]great
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]The donkeys loaded [C]with the bread
[Dm]Two hundred loaves are [Bb]spread
Rai[C]sins and fruit for [Dm]the men
Wine for the faint in the wilderness [Bb]then
Every[C]thing that belongs [Dm]to [C]Mep[Bb]hibosheth
Is [Gm]now yours [Am]to claim and to pos[Dm]sess
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]But Mephibos[C]heth came down low
[Dm]His feet untrimmed and clothes worn
He [Bb]said my servant [C]lied to you
He [Dm]left me lame and without [Bb]a clue
[C]I am like an [Dm]angel's friend
[Gm]Do whatev[Am7]er seems good [Dm]in the [Bb]end
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The don[C]keys loaded [Dm]with the bread
Two hundred loaves [Bb]are spread
Raisins [C]and fruit for [Dm]the men
Wine for the faint in the wilder[Bb]ness then
Ev[C]erything that be[Dm]longs [C]to [Bb]Mephibosheth
Is [Gm]now yours [Am]to claim and to pos[Dm]sess
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So you and [Bb]Zi[C]ba shall di[Dm]vide
[Bb]The land that [C]they are to a[Dm]bide
Divide [Bb]the [C]land and [Dm]be done
[Bb]The story of [Am]the servant [Dm]son
{end_of_verse}
